  "description": "DINQEY crystallizes in the tetragonal crystal system with space group P 42/n. Reported CIF formula moiety: C80 H76 Cl10 Co4 N10 O26 Y4,0.5(C2 H3 N1). From the CIF bond table, Y1 (Y) has 7 O neighbors; Y2 (Y) has 8 O neighbors; Co3 (Co) has 4 O neighbors; Co4 (Co) has 4 O neighbors; Y3 (Y) has 7 O neighbors; Y4 (Y) has 8 O neighbors; Co5 (Co) has 4 O neighbors; Co6 (Co) has 4 O neighbors. Oxygen-bridged metal-site graph: 13 pairs, 1 components; largest component is a network with cycles with approximately planar metal-site arrangement. Computed bridged metal-metal separations span 3.548-4.236 Å (not direct metal-metal bonds). Computed M-O-M angles span 94.62-129.11°; individual values and O labels are in metal_framework.links. Article card reports molecular formula [CoII4YIII4(OH)4(chp)10(acac)6]·0.5MeCN. Explicit grouped units in the article formula/name: 4 OH (explicit grouped unit in article formula). Article name explicitly identifies Co(II), Y(III).",
